the family acted?

443
00:17:11,206 --> 00:17:13,137
-Other than wanting my
son-in-law to diaper me, nope.

444
00:17:13,172 --> 00:17:14,965
-No. Same as always.

445
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,103
-When you were driving
out of town...

446
00:17:16,137 --> 00:17:17,448
-Nice likeness.
-...nothing out of the way

447
00:17:17,482 --> 00:17:19,793
in the street, the building
or the sky,

448
00:17:19,827 --> 00:17:22,206
no unusual lights,
some sound or...

449
00:17:22,241 --> 00:17:24,068
-Objection, your -- Oh.

450
00:17:24,103 --> 00:17:26,137
-Well, I heard something
that sounded like thunder.

451
00:17:26,172 --> 00:17:28,275
-Couldn't see it so good
because of the rain.

452
00:17:28,310 --> 00:17:29,724
-But it could be
a plane went over.

453
00:17:29,758 --> 00:17:32,379
-You are so high.
-All right, Dave.

454
00:17:32,413 --> 00:17:34,034
I can call on you again
if I need you?

455
00:17:34,068 --> 00:17:35,931
-Oh, yes.
-You know you can call me, Tad.

456
00:17:35,965 --> 00:17:37,482
-Edna?

457
00:17:37,517 --> 00:17:39,724
-My next guest, Rosemary!

458
00:17:39,758 --> 00:17:40,896
[Imitates cheering]

459
00:17:40,931 --> 00:17:42,068
-Is that
the telephone company's

460
00:17:42,103 --> 00:17:43,206
official transcripts?

461
00:17:43,241 --> 00:17:44,793
-It was a mistake.
I -- I didn't mean it!

462
00:17:44,827 --> 00:17:45,931
Oh.

463
00:17:45,965 --> 00:17:47,448
-The last call to Ludlow
was at 11:59 p.m.

464
00:17:47,482 --> 00:17:49,344
-When did you first notice
anything wrong

465
00:17:49,379 --> 00:17:51,103
