2052
01:17:50,862 --> 01:17:53,724
-Get me my little green shoes
with the curly toes.

2053
01:17:53,758 --> 01:17:57,034
-Oh, I love men
who use fairy-tale imagery.

2054
01:17:57,068 --> 01:18:01,413
♪♪

2055
01:18:01,448 --> 01:18:05,793
-♪ Dah, da-da-da-da-da-dah,
dah, da-da-da-da-dah ♪

2056
01:18:07,068 --> 01:18:08,620
-He just polygraphed
a sandwich.

2057
01:18:08,655 --> 01:18:10,000
He needs real help.

2058
01:18:10,034 --> 01:18:11,758
-I still don't understand.

2059
01:18:11,793 --> 01:18:13,172
Why didn't you put
the oscillator in the boat

2060
01:18:13,206 --> 01:18:15,344
in the first place
to send out the call?

2061
01:18:15,379 --> 01:18:16,862
Why attract them here?

2062
01:18:16,896 --> 01:18:17,862
-Because we'd never
get them all.

2063
01:18:17,896 --> 01:18:19,172
-Oh.

2064
01:18:19,206 --> 01:18:21,206
-Here, look.
-"Dilbert" is a scream today.

2065
01:18:21,241 --> 01:18:23,586
-Here we are in downtown
Chicago near the lake.

2066
01:18:23,620 --> 01:18:25,241
-Mm-hmm.
-Now, the locusts are scattered

2067
01:18:25,275 --> 01:18:27,724
all through the suburbs
and on the South Side.

2068
01:18:27,758 --> 01:18:29,275
-Hmm.
-We'll send out the call

2069
01:18:29,310 --> 01:18:30,551
from here.
-Yeah, but that's going

2070
01:18:30,586 --> 01:18:32,379
to attract them to us,
not into the water.

2071
01:18:32,413 --> 01:18:34,000
-Shut up.
-First of all, it's imperative

2072
01:18:34,034 --> 01:18:36,206
that every last one
of the locusts hear the call.

2073
01:18:36,241 --> 01:18:37,344
Now, in order to do that,

2074
01:18:37,379 --> 01:18:38,793
we've got to get
our amplifier speaker

2075
01:18:38,827 --> 01:18:41,620
at the highest possible point
to get maximum range.

2076
01:18:41,655 --> 01:18:43,448
Now we've got ours on the roof
of this building,

2077
01:18:43,482 --> 01:18:45,758
which is one of the tallest
in Chicago.

2078
01:18:45,793 --> 01:18:46,896
Now, once we get them here...

2079
01:18:46,931 --> 01:18:47,724
-Mm-hmm.
-I see.

2080
01:18:47,758 --> 01:18:48,827
Then the boat will take over.

2081
01:18:48,862 --> 01:18:50,310
-Exactly.

2082
01:18:50,344 --> 01:18:52,379
Once we have them in the heart
of the Loop, near our location,

2083
01:18:52,413 --> 01:18:54,965
they'll be within range
of the amplifier on the boat.

2084
01:18:55,000 --> 01:18:57,206
Now, we'll then radio
our oscillator signal

2085
01:18:57,241 --> 01:18:58,931
out to the boat,
and they, in turn,

2086
01:18:58,965 --> 01:19:00,965
will rebroadcast it
over their amplifier...

2087
01:19:01,000 --> 01:19:02,862
-You getting this?
-...attracting the locusts

2088
01:19:02,896 --> 01:19:05,896
to them and into the lake.

2089
01:19:06,965 --> 01:19:08,413
-We hope.
-You see?

2090
01:19:08,448 --> 01:19:11,241
That's what you do so well.
You cut me down.

2091
01:19:11,275 --> 01:19:14,379
-Will you check and see
about the temperature?

2092
01:19:14,413 --> 01:19:16,068
-I know a scientist
who needs a back rub.

2093
01:19:16,103 --> 01:19:18,034
-How can we be sure, sir?
-Hmm?

2094
01:19:18,068 --> 01:19:19,241
What do you mean?

2095
01:19:19,275 --> 01:19:21,310
-How can you know
that we'll get them all?

2096
01:19:21,344 --> 01:19:23,206
-Well, that's where
our observation posts

2097
01:19:23,241 --> 01:19:25,000
and the helicopter come in.

2098
01:19:25,034 --> 01:19:26,896
From their reports, we'll know
the exact location

2099
01:19:26,931 --> 01:19:30,758
of the locusts at all times
and if it's working.

2100
01:19:32,034 --> 01:19:34,206
-It's 70 degrees, Ed.
-Cooler near the lake.

2101
01:19:34,241 --> 01:19:36,793
-They're probably starting
to move.

2102
01:19:36,827 --> 01:19:39,034
-Emergency lab
to all observation posts.

2103
01:19:39,068 --> 01:19:41,172
Emergency lab to all
observation posts.

2104
01:19:41,206 --> 01:19:43,689
Report in, over.

2105
01:19:43,724 --> 01:19:45,137
-I'm hiding from a lion.

2106
01:19:45,172 --> 01:19:47,137
-Observation post number two
to emergency lab, over.

2107
01:19:47,172 --> 01:19:48,379
-It's got these women
scared stiff.

2108
01:19:48,413 --> 01:19:49,862
-What is your location?
Over.

2109
01:19:49,896 --> 01:19:52,379
-I'm situated in a store
across from the Art Institute

2110
01:19:52,413 --> 01:19:53,655
on Michigan Boulevard.

2111
01:19:53,689 --> 01:19:57,724
-Olga bras are on sale.
-Nothing in sight, out.

2112
01:19:57,758 --> 01:20:00,551
-Observation post number three
to emergency lab.

2113
01:20:00,586 --> 01:20:02,275
-I'm on the roof
of the Drayton Hotel.

2114
01:20:02,310 --> 01:20:03,862
-I see a huge
swirling crown rose.

2115
01:20:03,896 --> 01:20:05,103
-No sign of
grasshoppers in this area,

2116
01:20:05,137 --> 01:20:07,034
but the South Side's
getting some action.

2117
01:20:07,068 --> 01:20:09,068
-Wow.
-Out.

2118
01:20:09,103 --> 01:20:14,310
♪♪

2119
01:20:16,172 --> 01:20:19,172
-Emergency Lab to
observation post one.

2120
01:20:19,206 --> 01:20:21,896
Emergency Lab to
observation post one.

2121
01:20:21,931 --> 01:20:23,931
You did not report in.

2122
01:20:23,965 --> 01:20:25,103
What's your location, post one?

2123
01:20:25,137 --> 01:20:26,172
-Nothing going on here.

2124
01:20:26,206 --> 01:20:28,172
-This is observation
post number one.

2125
01:20:28,206 --> 01:20:29,724
I'm right in the middle of them!

2126
01:20:29,758 --> 01:20:33,172
I'm just south of 73rd
and South Shore Drive, out.

2127
01:20:33,206 --> 01:20:35,758
-Jimmy Fralic's mom says
I can stay for dinner.

2128
01:20:35,793 --> 01:20:38,206
-Emergency Lab
to helicopter, over.

2129
01:20:38,241 --> 01:20:40,896
-The name is Jeffrey.
I happen to be ina helicopter.

2130
01:20:40,931 --> 01:20:42,379
-Emergency lab,

2131
01:20:42,413 --> 01:20:45,310
the locusts are active
on the South Side of Chicago.

2132
01:20:45,344 --> 01:20:48,482
As yet, there are none
in the downtown area, out.

2133
01:20:48,517 --> 01:20:50,551
-Can you read me,
emergency lab?

2134
01:20:50,586 --> 01:20:51,620
Over.

2135
01:20:51,655 --> 01:20:52,896
-Yes, we can read you fine,
General.

2136
01:20:52,931 --> 01:20:55,000
Are you all set?
Over.

2137
01:20:56,068 --> 01:20:57,655
-Now, we're not
quite ready yet.

2138
01:20:57,689 --> 01:20:58,862
-Dummy here can't
fix the radio.

2139
01:20:58,896 --> 01:21:00,655
-I need you to hold off
a few more minutes.

2140
01:21:00,689 --> 01:21:02,689
-Come on.
-Over.

2141
01:21:02,724 --> 01:21:04,448
-I think we better start now,
General.

2142
01:21:04,482 --> 01:21:06,034
If they should change
their direction and start

2143
01:21:06,068 --> 01:21:09,620
moving away from Chicago,
we may not get them all, over.

2144
01:21:09,655 --> 01:21:12,482
-I don't like your starting
until we're completely ready.

2145
01:21:12,517 --> 01:21:14,413
This boat has to draw them
away from you

2146
01:21:14,448 --> 01:21:15,724
in a split second's notice.

2147
01:21:15,758 --> 01:21:18,137
-Ah, righty tighty.
-Over.

2148
01:21:18,172 --> 01:21:21,448
-I'd like to start, sir.

2149
01:21:21,482 --> 01:21:22,448
-Then go ahead.

2150
01:21:22,482 --> 01:21:24,655
-Baby.

2151
01:21:24,689 --> 01:21:27,448
-When I say, "Frog,"
that guy jumps.

2152
01:21:29,137 --> 01:21:31,551
-All right, I'm going to
polygraph my tie.

2153
01:21:31,586 --> 01:21:33,310
-Yes, sir?
-Is that the wire that leads

2154
01:21:33,344 --> 01:21:35,206
to the speaker on the roof?
-Sure.

2155
01:21:35,241 --> 01:21:36,758
-Well, plug it
into the amplifier, will you?

2156
01:21:36,793 --> 01:21:39,103
-Yes, sir.

2157
01:21:39,137 --> 01:21:41,413
-[Imitates electricity]
Aaaah!

2158
01:21:43,379 --> 01:21:45,379
[High-pitched whirring]

2159
01:21:45,413 --> 01:21:47,862
-All right! Playing Tull
out the window, man.

2160
01:21:47,896 --> 01:21:50,137
-Whoo!
-Whoo!

2161
01:21:50,172 --> 01:21:52,689
